{
  "id": "weekly-week-52-pay-friday",
  "source": "sars-guide:PAYE-GEN-01-G21 (2027) Rev 1 p. 9 (ANNUAL EQUIVALENT CALCULATION, Fourth Schedule para 9(1)/(2): remuneration x total pay periods in tax year / total pay periods worked; 52 weekly pay periods)",
  "sourceRef": "https://www.sars.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/Ops/Guides/PAYE-GEN-01-G21-Guide-for-Employers-iro-Employees-Tax-for-2027-External-Guide.pdf p. 9",
  "notes": "W1 (wave 7 W53) control for WEEK_53_PAY_DAY: the last pay day of a 52-payday year raises no warning (n = 52 = P). R3 000 a week, under 65, week Sat-Fri paid on the Friday: tax year 2027's Fridays run 6 March 2026 to 26 February 2027, 52 of them. Week 52 = 20-26 Feb 2027, after 51 weekly priors. Hand: AE = 3 000 x 52 = 156 000; tax 18% x 156 000 = 28 080 less the primary rebate 17 820 = 10 260 a year. Each prior's PAYE is the cumulative true-up round2(10 260 x k / 52 - the earlier priors' sum) (197.30 or 197.31), so the 51 priors sum to 10062.69; week 52 = 10 260 - 10062.69 = 197.31. UIF 1% of 3 000 = 30.00 (Feb's three earlier weeks R9 000 + R3 000, under the R17 712 month ceiling). Net 3 000 - 197.31 - 30.00 = 2772.69. expectedWarnings: none (HOURS_NOT_RECORDED is info, not asserted).",
